Note the doc comment on `mouse_shield_swallows` says "所以这里只认一个 bool,不认配置项" — with S①, now there IS a config item, but the *function* still only takes a bool (the mode decides who computes the bool). The doc says "不认配置项;开关由界面每帧按「映射开启 × FPS 模式生效 × 控制通道在线」重算". That's now outdated. The task says not to change capture.rs except if needed; updating this doc comment is appropriate since the semantics changed. I'll update that sentence to mention S① (mode → pure function in keymap) while keeping the "bool" interface. Careful about clippy `doc_lazy_continuation`/`doc list item without indentation` warnings — capture.rs's baseline already has one `this if statement can be collapsed` only. A new "doc list item without indentation" warning in capture.rs would be a NEW pair → must avoid! So I must be careful with doc comments in capture.rs: avoid lines starting with `- ` or a numbered list without indentation. Also avoid `too_many_arguments` (>7) and other lints.

I'll add to capture.rs:

```rust
/// 前台窗口所属进程的 pid(Windows 专有;拿不到一律 `None`)。
///
/// 用途(S①,用户 2026-10-11 第二个问题):判定"投屏窗口(scrcpy)是不是在前台"
/// —— 拿它跟 [`crate::adb::launch_scrcpy`] 保留的 scrcpy 子进程 pid 比较。
/// 用 pid 而不是窗口标题:标题随用户参数(`--window-title`)变,pidd 不会。
/// 拿不到(没有前台窗口 / 非 Windows / 没启动过 scrcpy)时调用方必须
/// **保守地不独占**(见 [`crate::keymap::mouse_shield_on`])。
#[cfg(windows)]
pub fn foreground_pid() -> Option<u32> {
    use windows_sys::Win32::UI::WindowsAndMessaging::{
        GetForegroundWindow, GetWindowThreadProcessId,
    };
    unsafe {
        let hwnd = GetForegroundWindow();
        if hwnd.is_null() {
            return None;
        }
        let mut pid = 0u32;
        GetWindowThreadProcessId(hwnd, &mut pid);
        (pid != 0).then_some(pid)
    }
}
```

Hmm "pidd" typo, fix.

Is `GetForegroundWindow` returning `HWND` = `*mut c_void`; `.is_null()` works. And `GetWindowThreadProcessId` returns u32.

Need to make sure the `windows_sys` import path is right: from line 2309 there's a use list with these two names — under which module path? Let me check line ~2300-2315 for the `use` block.

