Also add the waveform sanity test? The engine tests cover the wave behavior via recoil_tick. Maybe add a small direct test of `recoil_horizontal_wave` in engine for triangle shape. Optional; the engine test uses Sine only. Let me add a tiny engine test for triangle boundedness/shape? It'd be nice but not required. Actually requirement H① says "正弦/三角两种波形都要实现" — a test for triangle would strengthen. I'll add to the engine test file a compact test:

```rust
    #[test]
    fn recoil_horizontal_triangle_wave_matches_sine_phase() {
        let tau = std::f32::consts::TAU;
        // 起点、顶点、零点、谷值
        assert!((recoil_horizontal_wave(HorizontalWave::Triangle, 0.0)).abs() < 1e-6);
        assert!((recoil_horizontal_wave(HorizontalWave::Triangle, tau * 0.25) - 1.0).abs() < 1e-6);
        assert!((recoil_horizontal_wave(HorizontalWave::Triangle, tau * 0.5)).abs() < 1e-6);
        assert!((recoil_horizontal_wave(HorizontalWave::Triangle, tau * 0.75) + 1.0).abs() < 1e-6);
        // 与正弦同相:半个周期内三角是直线(中点 = 0.5·顶点)
        assert!((recoil_horizontal_wave(HorizontalWave::Triangle, tau * 0.125) - 0.5).abs() < 1e-6);
        assert!((recoil_horizontal_wave(HorizontalWave::Sine, tau * 0.25) - 1.0).abs() < 1e-6);
        // 有界:扫一个周期,处处在 ±1 内
        for k in 0..1000 {
            let p = tau * (k as f32) / 1000.0;
            for w in [HorizontalWave::Sine, HorizontalWave::Triangle] {
                assert!(recoil_horizontal_wave(w, p).abs() <= 1.0 + 1e-6, "{w:?} {p}");
            }
        }
    }
